        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Write down the formula for the area of a triangle.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=\\dfrac{bh}{2}$",
          "worked": "$$A=\\frac{bh}{2}$$\nHere $b$ is the base and $h$ is the perpendicular height.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-a2b32-p10-practice-slot-1-slot-1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "A triangular pennant has an area of $450\\text{ cm}^{2}$. Its height is twice its base. Find the base of the pennant, to 2 d.p.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$b\\approx21.21\\text{ cm}$",
          "worked": "The height is twice the base, so $h=2b$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{bh}{2}\\\\450&=\\frac{b(2b)}{2}\\\\450&=b^{2}\\\\b&=\\sqrt{450}\\\\b&\\approx21.21\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\nThe base must be positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
  },
